From c0ed82957c26234cd77ed3883211cf9be5a78a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 02:25:20 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] generic: standalone nft_flow_offload L2 bridge offload

Ship the nft_flow_offload bridge-offload series for pending-6.18 as
three consolidated patches (675-01 through 675-03), plus a
DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_KEEP_HW case addition in hack-6.18/650.  Uses native
NFPROTO_BRIDGE chain path (nft_do_chain_bridge) directly, eliminating
the kmod-br-netfilter dependency.  Bridged IP traffic traverses the
NFPROTO_BRIDGE NF_BR_FORWARD hook in __br_forward without any
netfilter involvement on the bridge family.

675-01: Kernel forward-path and bridge-VLAN infrastructure
----------------------------------------------------------
Exports __dev_fill_forward_path() accepting a caller-supplied
net_device_path_ctx, allowing callers to pre-populate context (e.g.
VLAN state) before the forward path walk.  The existing
dev_fill_forward_path() is refactored to wrap it.

Adds an exported bridge helper to br_vlan.c, declared via if_bridge.h:
  br_vlan_get_offload_info_rcu(): resolves the VLAN id for flow offload
  (skb VLAN tag id if present, PVID otherwise) and writes the bridge
  VLAN protocol to *proto.  Returns 0 when VLAN filtering is off or the
  device is not a bridge port.  Single br_port_get_rcu() lookup; must
  be called under RCU read lock.

Introduces DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_KEEP_HW path type for switchdev-backed
bridge ports where tagged VLANs are kept in hardware without software
stripping.  br_vlan_fill_forward_path_pvid() promotes switchdev-added
VLANs to KEEP_HW on the tagged path and to UNTAG_HW on the untagged
path; br_device.c treats KEEP_HW as a no-op like KEEP.

675-02: nft_flow_offload bridge offload + NFPROTO_BRIDGE flowtable type
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Core bridge offload in nft_flow_offload.c / nf_flow_table_path.c:

  - nft_flow_route() renamed to nft_flow_route_routing() with a null-dst
    guard to prevent kernel panics when no L3 route exists for a bridged
    interface.

  - nft_flow_route_bridging() allocates minimal dst entries anchored to
    the bridge master device, avoiding nf_route() which fails for
    bridged-only prefixes.  Both directions share one dst via
    dst_hold(); dsts are released on error paths to prevent memory leaks.

  - nft_dev_forward_path() copies MAC addresses from the packet header
    for bridged flows, with conntrack-direction-aware source/dest swap.
    Bridge-port ingress devices try the L2 bridge path first via
    nft_flow_route_bridging(); on failure (no FDB entry, no bridge
    master, dst alloc failure) the route is zeroed and L3 routing is
    retried via nft_flow_route_routing(), eliminating the TOCTOU race
    of a speculative FDB probe.

  - nft_dev_forward_path() pre-fills VLAN context for hardware offload
    entries: br_vlan_get_offload_info_rcu() resolves the port via
    br_port_get_rcu() and the VLAN id/proto from the skb VLAN tag (or
    the port PVID via br_vlan_get_pvid_rcu() when the packet is
    untagged), populating ctx.vlan[] and info.encap[] (guarded by
    NF_FLOW_TABLE_ENCAP_MAX); when VLAN filtering is off, the skb VLAN
    tag is recorded as passthrough encap.

  - info->indev hoisted outside the path-type switch so bridge ingress
    device is tracked for all path types.

  - DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_UNTAG underflow fixed: check num_encaps == 0
    before decrementing, avoiding u8 wraparound to 255.

  - info->xmit_type = FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_DIRECT scoped to DEV_PATH_BRIDGE
    and DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA only; ETHERNET/VLAN/PPPOE paths retain
    FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH for software flow offload.

  - DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA handled in nft_dev_path_info() to populate the
    correct source device for the MediaTek PPE offload path.

  - nft_flow_validate() accepts NFPROTO_BRIDGE for bridge-family chains.

  - L3 protocol derived from ct->tuplehash[dir].tuple.src.l3num instead
    of nft_pf(pkt) which returns NFPROTO_BRIDGE in bridge-family tables.

Registers an NFPROTO_BRIDGE flowtable type in nf_flow_table_inet.ko,
reusing the inet flowtable hook (nf_flow_offload_inet_hook, which strips
VLAN/PPPoE encapsulation and dispatches to the IPv4 or IPv6 offload
hooks, with routing selected by the flow tuple L3 protocol via
nf_flow_rule_route_inet) and a MODULE_ALIAS_NF_FLOWTABLE(AF_BRIDGE) so
nft can autoload the module.  This allows nftables flowtable
declarations in bridge-family tables, replacing the kmod-br-netfilter
(CONFIG_BRIDGE_NETFILTER) approach of lifting bridged IP traffic into
the inet forward chain.  No separate kmod is produced; kmod-nft-offload
carries the bridge flowtable support via nf_flow_table_inet.ko.

675-03: nf_conntrack_bridge VLAN/PPPoE support
------------------------------------------------
Adds nf_ct_bridge_inner() for parsing a single outer VLAN tag or PPPoE
encapsulation (optionally with one inner VLAN tag inside the PPPoE
frame), extends nf_bridge_frag_data with VLAN/PPPoE state, and adds
defrag/refrag/frag_restore handling for bridged packets with these
encapsulations.  PPP protocol ids are translated to ethertypes for the
inner IP/IPv6 switch, and frag state is saved before the MAC headers
are pulled.

